  "notes": [
    "Step 5 Chat classification reconciles exactly to the 53 documented enum names: 13 mapped/handled + 8 explicit no-op + 2 suppressed raw-reasoning + 1 lifecycle notification (response.queued) + 29 rejected specialized = 53. The 11 explicitly non-content acceptances are the 8 NOOP_EVENTS, response.reasoning_text.delta/done and response.queued; queued is a lifecycle notification, not a no-op.",
    "response.queued requires an object payload.response, captures response id/created_at for identity exactly as response.created does, emits no Chat role chunk and is not terminal. response.created and response.in_progress behavior is unchanged.",
    "response.reasoning_text.delta validates delta and response.reasoning_text.done validates text as strings, then discards them. Raw reasoning is never surfaced as Chat content or reasoning_content, never stored, and never logged; a malformed string still fails. This suppression is a separately named set, not NOOP_EVENTS.",
    "Any other name is still rejected as unsupported_sse_event; there is no blanket catch-all. On a named Chat stream failure the thrown error may carry only a bounded eventName (1-128 characters of [A-Za-z0-9_.-], never a configured secret) for the request log. Payloads, text, reasoning, tool data and raw provider messages are never logged, and the client-facing error envelope does not gain payload data.",
    "The current Chat parser also recognizes response.cancelled as a compatibility terminal despite that name not appearing in this documented enum; the API event inventory remains exactly 53 names.",
    "Transport for all documented events is implemented and tested offline. Native creation is implemented default-off with the initial text/reasoning/function policy; specialized feature activation remains pending. Schema/event enumeration does not establish live resource/model/version/region/deployment support.",
    "Azure's Responses how-to currently says image generation using multi-turn editing and streaming is not supported; corresponding enum events stay explicitly feature-gated pending verified deployment support."
  ]
